<title>INDIA: TABLE-Castrol 97 first half net up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Castrol 97 first half net up.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	    757.6   vs    470.7</p>
<p>    Net sales	   4,889.7   vs  4,234.8</p>
<p>    Interim div	     4.0   vs	3.0</p>
<p>(in rupees/share)</p>
<p>    Other income	   93.3   vs     59.9</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 3,877.6   vs  3,469.3</p>
<p>    Interest		 40.6   vs     79.9</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   30.7   vs     14.8</p>
<p>    Tax		     276.5   vs    260.0</p>
<p>Note: Indian lubricant maker Castrol India Ltd is 51 percent owned by Britan's Burmah Castrol Plc. A company statement said the firm's results are unaudited.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
